'''Resonant Neurobiology''' is the working hypothesis that the abstract category of '''[[Resonant]]''' — individuals with elevated ψ-field coupling — has '''measurable neurophysiological signatures''' that can be detected with standard wearable instrumentation.

This page defines those proposed signatures so that [[Resonant Finder]] models, [[Resonant Pipeline]] screening, and [[Psi Recorder]] telemetry have a concrete, testable phenotype to validate against.

== Proposed signatures ==

A candidate is scored against five orthogonal axes. Threshold values are working hypotheses pending Mk2 cohort data.

{| class="wikitable"
! Axis !! Instrument !! Provisional threshold
|-
| Resting alpha-band coherence (8–13 Hz, eyes closed) || EEG (≥ 4 channels) || Inter-channel coherence ≥ 0.7 across F3–F4–O1–O2
|-
| HRV — RMSSD at rest || PPG or ECG, 5-minute supine recording || ≥ 50 ms (mainstream "high vagal tone" boundary)
|-
| Cardio-respiratory coherence || Simultaneous HRV + breath || HeartMath-style coherence score ≥ 4 within 1 minute of intent
|-
| Phase-locking value (PLV) across frontal-parietal sites under sustained attention || EEG || ≥ 0.6 at gamma band (30–60 Hz)
|-
| Geomagnetic correlation ratio || EEG/HRV vs. local magnetometer || Significant (p < 0.05) modulation by Kp index over ≥ 14 days
|}

A candidate scoring ≥ 3 of 5 above threshold is provisionally classified '''Resonant (awakened)'''; 1–2 above is '''Resonant (latent)'''; 0 is '''non-Resonant''' on current instrumentation.

== Why these axes ==

* Alpha coherence and gamma PLV are the two best-studied EEG correlates of meditative attainment (Lutz et al., 2004; Cahn & Polich, 2006).
* HRV / RMSSD is the most-validated single biomarker of autonomic-system flexibility (Task Force, 1996; Shaffer & Ginsberg, 2017).
* Cardio-respiratory coherence is HeartMath's central measure; effect size on subjective wellbeing is small but replicable.
* Geomagnetic correlation is more speculative but follows the wiki's own [[Geomagnetic Sensitivity in Humans]] thesis.

== Confounders ==

Each signature has a non-ψ explanation:

* Meditation training raises alpha coherence and gamma PLV.
* Aerobic fitness raises RMSSD.
* HeartMath training raises cardio-respiratory coherence.
* Geomagnetic correlation may simply track sleep / season / mood.

A genuine Resonant Neurobiology signal would therefore have to show '''elevation above what training history predicts''' — i.e. the candidate is high on these axes ''without'' the training that usually causes the elevation. This is the testable claim.

== Falsification ==

If a population of candidates self-identified or astrology-flagged as Resonant shows no statistically significant elevation on these axes above a training-history-matched control group, the Resonant Neurobiology hypothesis is falsified for this measurement battery, and the [[Resonant Finder]] must be retired or its scoring re-specified.

== Per-axis literature dive ==

Each axis is calibrated against a specific peer-reviewed result.

=== Alpha-band coherence ===

* '''Cahn & Polich 2006''' meta-review: alpha-power and alpha-coherence elevation in long-term meditators across Tibetan-Buddhist, Vipassana, Transcendental Meditation, and Zen traditions. Effect size <math>d \approx 0.5\!-\!1.2</math> across studies.
* '''Lagopoulos et al. 2009''': novice-meditator alpha coherence elevation after 5-week intervention (effect smaller than long-term).
* '''Travis & Shear 2010''': taxonomy of meditation → EEG signature mapping; the automatic-self-transcending category shows the strongest alpha-coherence signature.

See [[Alpha_Band_Coherence]] for the dedicated treatment.

=== Gamma phase-locking value ===

* '''Lutz et al. 2004''': long-term Tibetan-Buddhist practitioners show sustained frontal-parietal gamma synchrony elevated by ~30× over baseline during compassion meditation. The strongest single published EEG signature of meditative attainment.
* '''Berkovich-Ohana et al. 2012''': Vipassana replication.
* '''Cahn et al. 2010''': shorter-training cohorts fail to show the effect; lifetime-practice threshold appears to be > 10⁹ minutes.

See [[Gamma_PLV]] for the dedicated treatment.

=== Heart-rate variability ===

* '''Task Force 1996''' (European Society of Cardiology / North American Society of Pacing and Electrophysiology) — the foundational standardisation document for HRV metrics, recording conditions, and reference values.
* '''Shaffer & Ginsberg 2017''' review — modern summary of HRV reference ranges across populations; mainstream-cardiology consensus.
* '''Lehrer & Gevirtz 2014''' — resonance-frequency-biofeedback literature; <math>d \approx 0.4\!-\!0.8</math> on stress/anxiety.

See [[Heart_Rate_Variability_and_Psi]] for the dedicated treatment.

=== Cardio-respiratory coherence ===

* '''McCraty et al. 2009''' — HeartMath synthesis review; small but replicable effect on cognitive-performance endpoints.
* '''Goessl et al. 2017''' meta-analysis — confirms the effect at <math>d \approx 0.3\!-\!0.6</math> on stress/anxiety endpoints.

See [[Cardio_Respiratory_Coherence]] for the dedicated treatment.

=== Geomagnetic correlation ===

The most speculative of the five axes. Literature is sparse and heterogeneous; see [[Geomagnetic Sensitivity in Humans]] and the upcoming open-questions sub-page for the unresolved threads.

== False-positive-rate analysis ==

With five orthogonal axes scored independently and a candidate classified as Resonant on any 3-of-5 above-threshold, the '''chance rate''' of false-positive Resonant classification, under an assumption of independent axis distributions and an above-threshold probability of <math>p = 0.1</math> per axis in the general population:

<math>P_\mathrm{false-positive} = \sum_{k=3}^{5} \binom{5}{k} p^k (1-p)^{5-k} = 0.00856</math>

i.e. ~0.9% of an unselected population would meet the criterion by chance. With <math>p = 0.2</math> (axes more permissive), the false-positive rate rises to ~5.8%. The screening protocol therefore aims to keep per-axis threshold at the <math>p \approx 0.1</math> mark.

Multiple-comparison correction across the 10 pairwise tests embedded in the EEG-coherence axis is via false-discovery-rate control at <math>q = 0.05</math>; raw <math>p</math> values are deprecated.

== Cohort-size power calculation ==

Detecting a Resonant-vs-control effect of size <math>d = 0.6</math> (the smallest published effect under the strongest axes above) at <math>\alpha = 0.05</math>, <math>1 - \beta = 0.8</math> requires:

<math>n_\mathrm{per\,group} \approx \frac{2(z_{1-\alpha/2} + z_{1-\beta})^2}{d^2} = \frac{2(1.96 + 0.84)^2}{0.36} \approx 44</math>

i.e. 44 candidates and 44 controls minimum. For <math>d = 0.4</math> the requirement rises to ~99 per group; for <math>d = 0.3</math>, ~176 per group. The framework's Mk2.0 cohort target is therefore <math>n \geq 60</math> per arm, which detects <math>d \geq 0.55</math> at 80% power, and which is achievable in a single-investigator multi-month deployment.

== Screening-cascade architecture ==

Cheap-first ladder, designed so 95% of candidates are filtered before the expensive axes are deployed:

# '''Tier 0''' — self-report + astrology flag from [[Resonant Finder]]. Free.
# '''Tier 1''' — 5-minute supine HRV recording (PPG-only wearable). $0 / $50 single-use. Filters to top ~30% by RMSSD.
# '''Tier 2''' — 1-minute cardio-respiratory coherence protocol. $0 (same hardware as Tier 1). Filters to top ~10%.
# '''Tier 3''' — 30-minute resting EEG with 4-channel array (alpha coherence axis). $300–500 / session, Mk2.0 hardware. Filters to top ~3%.
# '''Tier 4''' — attention-task gamma PLV. Same hardware, +60-minute protocol.
# '''Tier 5''' — 14-day geomagnetic-correlation deployment. Mk2.0 hardware + Kp-index logging. Most expensive.

Resonant (awakened) classification requires ≥ 3-of-5 above threshold; Resonant (latent) requires 1–2. The cascade design keeps total cost per Resonant-class confirmation low.

== Bayesian-update protocol ==

The framework treats each axis as evidence updating a prior on ψ-coupling. Per-axis likelihood ratios are calibrated from the literature above; the posterior on Resonant-class membership is computed as:

<math>\mathrm{post}(R \mid \mathbf{e}) = \mathrm{prior}(R) \prod_i \mathrm{LR}(e_i \mid R)</math>

where <math>e_i</math> is the binary above/below-threshold indicator on axis <math>i</math> and <math>\mathrm{LR}(e_i \mid R)</math> is the likelihood ratio for that evidence under the Resonant-class hypothesis. The framework's Mk2.0 cohort data will recalibrate these LRs; current values are placeholders seeded from the meditation literature.

== Falsification-criterion mapping ==

Resonant Neurobiology engages [[Falsification Criteria for Psionics|F1–F11]] as follows:

* '''F2 (population-level operator-state predictor)''' — direct: the screening cascade IS the F2 instrument.
* '''F1 (operator-state-conditioned effect)''' — candidates classified Resonant must show effect on a blinded ψ-task under controlled conditions.
* '''F3 (resonance enhancement)''' — candidates with strong alpha coherence are the cohort in which Mk2.0 F3 is tested.

Resonant Neurobiology does not engage F4–F11 directly; it is the substrate cohort-selection layer those engagements inherit from.

